{
  "_readme": {
    "purpose": "Auto-caption mistranscriptions of trading jargon, and their corrections. YouTube's ASR was not trained on ICT/SMC vocabulary, so it substitutes common English words that sound similar -- 'choch' becomes 'chalk', 'order block' becomes 'order lock'. Left uncorrected, a RAG query for 'CHoCH' misses every auto-captioned video that discussed it.",
    "applied_to": "cleaned_text ONLY. raw_text is never modified, so every substitution stays auditable and a wrong rule here can be found and undone without re-scraping.",
    "matching": "case-insensitive, whole-word (\\b...\\b). Longest keys are replaced first, so 'fair value gap' is corrected before any rule touching 'gap' alone can interfere.",
    "caution": "Only add a mapping whose WRONG side is unambiguous in a trading transcript. 'gold' -> 'GOLD' would be safe; 'range' -> anything would not, because 'range' is also ordinary English. A bad rule here silently corrupts every future embedding."
  },

